      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “irreversible coma” as having “no realistic chance of recovery.” It only states more generally that decisions occur when patients “have little hope of recovery,” without tying that phrasing specifically to irreversible coma.",
        "While the packet does mention that, under Taiwan’s PRAA/ACP legal framework, individuals can authorize withholding/withdrawal of life-sustaining treatment and artificial nutrition and hydration in situations “like irreversible coma,” it does not explicitly frame this as “in advance care planning” a person “may choose in advance to forgo” those treatments in the exact manner stated in the definition."
